troparionGlory.text:
In their sufferings, Thy martyrs O Lord,
received imperishable crowns from Thee, our God;
for, possessed of Thy might,
they set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons.//
By their supplications save Thou our souls.

ode4.irmos2:
O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation;
I have considered Thy works,//
and I have glorified Thy Divinity.

ode6.irmos2:
I will pour out my prayer unto the Lord,
and to Him will I proclaim my grief;
for my soul is filled with evils,
and my life unto Hades hath drawn nigh,
and like Jonah I pray unto Thee:
Raise me up from corruption, O God.

ode9.irmos2:
Every ear is awestruck at hearing of God's ineffable condescension,
for the Most High voluntarily descended and assumed flesh,
becoming man in the Virgin's womb;
wherefore we the faithful magnify//
the most pure Theotokos.

bothNow.text:
We hymn thee, the Mother and Virgin, O all-immaculate one;
for in thy womb thou didst bear the God of all;
and professing His unity to be immutable in His hypostasis,
we who because of thee are saved,//
confess thee to be the Theotokos and Sovereign Lady.
